RESPONSE

P-011 PATCH — Autonomous Ingestion with Governance-First Bounded Growth

Objective

Introduce controlled autonomous ingestion across JARVIS + AYRE using existing infrastructure (GitHub + Supabase MCP bridge), while enforcing strict no-drift / no-unvalidated-write rules.


---

1. Patch Scope

In Scope

Autonomous collection

Delta-based ingestion

Classification + routing

Queue-based memory staging

Claude Code implementation delegation


Out of Scope

New god systems

Direct memory writes from external sources

Continuous uncontrolled crawling

Schema expansion without dependency mapping



---

2. Core Architectural Flow (P-011)

External Sources
    ↓
Collection Layer (AYRE-driven triggers or schedules)
    ↓
Delta Extractor (change detection only)
    ↓
ERIS (noise filter + entropy scoring)
    ↓
ATHENA (classification + routing decision)
    ↓
Staging Queue (Supabase)
    ↓
Validation Gate (JARVIS / optional human approval)
    ↓
MNEMOS / MIMIR (approved write only)
    ↓
GitHub Commit (canonical trace log)


---

3. Two-Mode Ingestion System

MODE A — Passive Collection (AYRE)

Purpose: discovery + signal gathering

RSS feeds

GitHub releases

API updates

Selected web sources

Repo activity tracking


Rules:

No persistence to canonical memory

Only emits "candidates"


Output:

Candidate Object:
- source
- timestamp
- extracted delta
- relevance score
- confidence


---

MODE B — Structured Ingestion (JARVIS)

Purpose: controlled memory formation

Rules:

Only accepts deltas from staging queue

Requires ATHENA classification

Must pass ERIS filter threshold

Must be traceable to source hash


Output types:

Knowledge node

Graph edge update

Versioned memory patch



---

4. Governance Constraints (Hard Rules)

G1 — No Autonomous Write

External data cannot directly modify MNEMOS or MIMIR

G2 — Delta Only Storage

Store changes, not full documents

G3 — Traceability Requirement

Every stored node must include:

source_id
hash
ingestion_time
pipeline_path
validation_status


---

G4 — Complexity Budget

Any new ingestion component must satisfy:

added_complexity <= removed_complexity

If violated → reject or merge into existing system.


---

5. Supabase Role (Operational Memory Layer)

Supabase becomes:

INGESTION_QUEUE TABLE
- raw_delta
- classification_status
- ERIS_score
- ATHENA_tag
- approval_state
- retry_count

Also:

staging buffer

audit trail

replay system



---

6. GitHub Role (Canonical Truth Layer)

GitHub stores:

Approved memory commits

Patch history

Schema evolution logs

Ingestion pipeline versions


Structure:

/jarvis/memory/approved/
/jarvis/memory/rejected/
/jarvis/ingestion/pipelines/
/jarvis/audit/logs/


